        "TESTSUITE_DB_PORT: when the user enters nothing or 'null', the value is written as bare `null`; any digit string is written as a bare integer — both satisfy the AC.",
        "composer.json scripts section: the new 'setup' entry is the last script before the closing brace — valid JSON confirmed.",
        "Idempotency relies on parseExistingDbConfig() / parseExistingUiConfig() which read the already-generated config files (not the dist files) if they exist. The extractConstantValue() regex handles all three value shapes the script itself writes.",
        "SIGINT handler restores `stty echo` if the user hits Ctrl+C during a password prompt — requires the pcntl extension (guarded with function_exists)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-06T08:47:31Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 9 acceptance criteria confirmed met. Syntax valid, logic verified via isolated function tests.",
        "Minor observations (all low priority, non-blocking): (1) non-numeric port input casts to 0 silently; (2) empty-password idempotency is functionally correct but not distinguishable from default; (3) schema import always runs on re-setup — idempotency depends on SQL DDL guards in testsuite.sql.",
        "Security auditor should review: (a) SQL injection risk in ensureDatabase() — $dbName is taken from user input and interpolated into backtick-quoted CREATE DATABASE / USE statements; (b) password written in plaintext to test-db-config.php; (c) shell_exec('stty ...') usage in promptPassword."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-06T08:48:44Z",
      "notes": [
        "Security audit PASS. 0 Critical, 0 High findings. Three Medium items documented (SQL identifier interpolation in ensureDatabase, plaintext password in generated config file, shell_exec for stty terminal control) — all contextually acceptable for a local-only developer CLI tool with no remote attack surface. Three Low/Info observations also recorded. All 9 acceptance criteria confirmed met. No remediation required before code review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Reviewer",
      "to_agent": "Documentation",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-06T08:50:37Z",
      "notes": [
        "Code review PASS. Three Fix-Forward changes applied (all non-behavioral, syntax verified clean): (1) stty availability comment clarification in cli-utilities.php; (2) addslashes() scope comment in replaceConfigConstant(); (3) file_put_contents() return-value error checks in generateDbConfig() and generateUiConfig() — previously silent failures now produce a user-facing error and exit(1).",
        "One [documentation-forward] item for the Documentation agent: confirm test-db-config.php and test-ui-config.php are in .gitignore and document this in the README/contributor guide.",
        "All 9 acceptance criteria confirmed met. No blocking issues. WP is ready for the Documentation pipeline."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

